#N canvas 0 50 1040 950 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   freeze~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 spectral freeze;
#X text 30 86 holds the spectrum of the incoming sound and keeps it sounding after the input stops. jitter and shimmer keep the held sound alive, f 110;
#X text 30 146 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 190 a short time fourier transform (2048 points and 75 percent overlap and a hann window) splits the sound into frames. while frozen one frame is repeated with random phase and level changes so the held sound does not sound static, f 110;
#X text 30 270 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 314 1  open the engine page and switch the sound on, f 110;
#X text 30 344 2  set freeze to on and then switch the sound off. the held sound keeps playing, f 110;
#X text 30 374 3  move jitter and shimmer to change how static the held sound is, f 110;
#X text 30 404 everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy. every effect has presets and a and b morph and mutate and a data inlet, f 110;
#X text 30 464 try:  latency is the fft size (2048 samples). send size 4096 for a smoother hold, f 110;
#X text 30 494 try:  freeze can be mapped to nothing but mix and jitter can be mapped to data, f 110;
#X text 30 538 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 582 no sound: the effect has a delay of one fft size and needs dsp on, f 110;
#X text 30 612 clicks when freeze is switched: the release is short on purpose. use mix to blend, f 110;
#X text 30 642 names: give every instance its own name as the first argument like [tessera/freeze~ f1]. the name is also the stash namespace, f 110;
#X text 30 706 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 906 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 factory sounds are stored as plain text. click a box to load that sound. every slider in the effect follows, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; f1 preset 0;
#X text 240 112 0  default;
#X msg 30 144 \; f1 preset 1;
#X text 240 146 1  pure drone;
#X msg 30 178 \; f1 preset 2;
#X text 240 180 2  airy hold;
#X msg 460 110 \; f1 preset 3;
#X text 670 112 3  glitter;
#X msg 460 144 \; f1 preset 4;
#X text 670 146 4  dust cloud;
#X msg 460 178 \; f1 preset 5;
#X text 670 180 5  live blend;
#X text 30 232 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 276 20 0 0 0 - f1-name -;
#X floatatom 230 276 4 0 0 0 - f1-index -;
#X text 340 278 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 320 \; f1 next;
#X msg 142 320 \; f1 prev;
#X msg 254 320 \; f1 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 360 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1. mutate leaves mix and level alone, f 100;
#X text 30 410 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 454 \; f1 A;
#X msg 118 454 \; f1 B;
#X text 206 456 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 496 morph;
#X obj 110 494 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 f1-morph empty empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 538 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every continuous parameter blends smoothly. switches change at the middle, f 100;
#X text 30 588 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 632 \; f1 store mysound;
#X msg 214 632 \; f1 save my.bank;
#X msg 390 632 \; f1 load my.bank;
#X text 30 672 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load reads such a file, f 100;
#X text 30 722 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 766 every slider of the effect sends to f1-param and listens on f1-param-r. this is the naming scheme of the stash preset library: create [stash/bank f1] and send it a scan message with the name of the patch that holds the effect. it follows the stash rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 750 pd presets;
#X text 30 784 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1200 394 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every parameter is also a message: [name value( in real units or for a switch the option name or number. the controls in the effect panel and these messages do the same, f 120;
#X text 30 66 parameter;
#X text 210 66 values;
#X text 560 66 what it does;
#X text 30 100 freeze;
#X text 210 100 off | on, f 36;
#X text 560 100 on holds the current spectrum, f 54;
#X text 30 136 jitter;
#X text 210 136 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 136 random phase of every frame. 0 is a pure drone and higher is airier, f 54;
#X text 30 192 shimmer;
#X text 210 192 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 192 random level of every bin. a slow glittering movement, f 54;
#X text 30 248 mix;
#X text 210 248 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 248 0 is the dry sound and 1 is only the effect, f 54;
#X text 30 294 any continuous parameter can be driven by data: send datamap name amount and then data 0 to 1. see the messages page, f 120;
#X restore 220 750 pd parameters;
#X text 220 784 every control, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 766 messages 0;
#X text 30 16 click any box to send it to the effect. the effect listens to its name so you can use [s f1] from anywhere in your patch, f 110;
#X text 30 66 message;
#X text 430 66 what it does;
#X msg 30 100 \; f1 params;
#X text 430 102 prints every parameter and its range in the console, f 76;
#X msg 30 134 \; f1 preset 3;
#X text 430 136 loads preset 3 (or a preset by name: preset pure drone), f 76;
#X msg 30 168 \; f1 next;
#X text 430 170 next preset (wraps around), f 76;
#X msg 30 202 \; f1 prev;
#X text 430 204 previous preset, f 76;
#X msg 30 236 \; f1 mutate 0.4;
#X text 430 238 random variation of the current sound. 0 is nothing and 1 is a lot, f 76;
#X msg 30 270 \; f1 A;
#X text 430 272 remember the current sound as a, f 76;
#X msg 30 304 \; f1 B;
#X text 430 306 remember the current sound as b, f 76;
#X msg 30 338 \; f1 morph 0.5;
#X text 430 340 blend between a and b from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 372 \; f1 data 0.7;
#X text 430 374 data inlet: a value from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 406 \; f1 datamap jitter 0.5;
#X text 430 408 map the data inlet to a continuous parameter. 0.5 means the full range of the parameter at data 0 and 1. amount 0 removes the mapping. up to four mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 480 \; f1 datamap clear;
#X text 430 482 remove all data mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 514 \; f1 store mysound;
#X text 430 516 keep the current sound in the user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 548 \; f1 save my.bank;
#X text 430 550 write the user bank to a text file, f 76;
#X msg 30 582 \; f1 load my.bank;
#X text 430 584 read a user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 616 \; f1 size 4096;
#X text 430 618 fft size 256 to 16384 (latency equals the size), f 76;
#X msg 30 650 \; f1 reset;
#X text 430 652 clears the buffers, f 76;
#X msg 30 684 \; f1 latency;
#X text 430 686 prints the delay in the console, f 76;
#X restore 410 750 pd messages;
#X text 410 784 clickable list, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1000 examples 0;
#X text 30 16 copy these into your own patch. they all talk to the effect through [s f1] so the engine page must be open with dsp on, f 130;
#X text 30 56 1  walk through the presets;
#X obj 30 90 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 30 130 metro 2500;
#X obj 30 170 random 6;
#X obj 30 210 list prepend preset;
#X obj 30 250 list trim;
#X obj 30 290 s f1;
#X text 330 56 2  slow morph between preset 0 and 1;
#X msg 330 90 \; f1 preset 0 \; f1 A \; f1 preset 1 \; f1 B;
#X obj 330 150 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 330 190 metro 6000;
#X msg 330 230 0 \, 1 3000 \, 0 3000 3000;
#X obj 330 270 line 0 30;
#X obj 330 310 list prepend morph;
#X obj 330 350 list trim;
#X obj 330 390 s f1;
#X text 740 56 3  sweep jitter with a ramp;
#X obj 740 90 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 740 130 metro 4000;
#X msg 740 170 0 \, 1 2000 \, 0 2000 2000;
#X obj 740 210 line 0 30;
#X obj 740 250 list prepend jitter;
#X obj 740 290 list trim;
#X obj 740 330 s f1;
#X text 30 496 4  data in: a ramp stands in for a sensor or a csv column. click the map box once first;
#X msg 30 530 \; f1 datamap jitter 0.4;
#X obj 30 570 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 30 610 metro 4000;
#X msg 30 650 0 \, 1 2000 \, 0 2000 2000;
#X obj 30 690 line 0 30;
#X obj 30 730 list prepend data;
#X obj 30 770 list trim;
#X obj 30 810 s f1;
#X text 330 570 in your own patch send any value from 0 to 1 to [s f1] as: data 0.7. for a csv series scale it to the range 0 to 1 first. [tessera/datamod~] does that for you and its data outlet can be connected straight to the inlet of any tessera effect, f 70;
